From: Pharma360 QA Team
Subject: [PATCH 006/05] Remove unnecessary build-essential from backend Dockerfile
Date: 2026-11-01

This patch removes the build-essential package from the backend Dockerfile.
All Python dependencies in requirements.txt are pre-compiled (psycopg2-binary,
not psycopg2), so build-essential (gcc, make, g++) is not needed.

This reduces:
- Image size
- Build time
- Potential security vulnerabilities

---
 docker/backend.Dockerfile | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 0 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docker/backend.Dockerfile b/docker/backend.Dockerfile
index abc1234..def5678 100644
--- a/docker/backend.Dockerfile
+++ b/docker/backend.Dockerfile
@@ -17,9 +17,6 @@ FROM python:3.11-slim-bookworm as builder
 # Configuration du builder
 WORKDIR /app
 
-# Installer les d\u00e9pendances de build
-RUN apt-get update && \\
-    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\
-    build-essential \\
-    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
-
 # Copier les fichiers de d\u00e9pendances
 COPY backend/requirements.txt ./
 
---
To apply this patch:
  cd /workspace/github__DuDuEZN__Pharma-360
  patch -p1 < patches/006-fix-backend-dockerfile-remove-build-essential.patch

OR manually apply:
  1. Edit docker/backend.Dockerfile
  2. Remove lines 20-23 (the apt-get install build-essential block)

Note: This optimization is optional. The backend will work with or without
this change, but removing build-essential makes the image smaller and faster to build.
